  "index": 1,
  "response": "The main points of the two passages are:\n\n1. The exploitation of indigenous people for their labor and resources:\n\t* In Peru, the mita system requires Indians to work in mines every two months, earning 4 reals per day.\n\t* In Siberia, the local Yakut and Tungus natives are forced to pay yasak tribute in the form of furbearing animals, which have become scarce due to overhunting.\n2. The negative impact of these practices on the indigenous populations:\n\t* In Peru, the mita system is described as \"distressing\" and causing \"great confusion.\"\n\t* In Siberia, the lack of horses has made it difficult for natives to hunt, leading to food shortages.\n3. The role of colonial powers in perpetuating these practices:\n\t* In Peru, the mita system is enforced by His Majesty's warrant, highlighting the authority of the colonial power over indigenous peoples.\n\t* In Siberia, the yasak tribute is collected by colonial officials, further emphasizing their control over the native population.",
